WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
Field devices form the connection between digital control and the physical process.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.120
Sensors measure conditions such as temperature, pressure, flow, level, speed, vibration,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.435
or position.

00:00:10.435 --> 00:00:11.970
Instrumentation may condition, convert,

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.600
or transmit those measurements so a controller can use them reliably.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.365
Actuators perform physical work in response to control signals.

00:00:18.365 --> 00:00:21.280
A valve actuator changes flow, a motor drives machinery,

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.755
a variable-frequency drive adjusts speed, and a relay changes an electrical circuit.

00:00:25.755 --> 00:00:30.570
Some devices combine measurement, local logic, diagnostics, and actuation in one package.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.500
Field signals may be discrete, indicating states such as open or closed, or analog,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.240
representing a range of values.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:40.600
They can travel through direct input and output wiring, serial links, fieldbus networks,

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.200
industrial Ethernet, or gateways.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.055
The architecture must account for both networked devices and equipment that never appears

00:00:46.055 --> 00:00:47.920
as a conventional IP endpoint.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.160
Field-device integrity is essential because bad data can lead to a bad control decision,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.520
while an incorrect output can affect equipment immediately.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.600
A failed sensor, wiring problem, calibration error, configuration mistake,

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.960
or cyber event may produce similar symptoms.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.400
Diagnosis requires process history, device health, controller evidence,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.275
and physical inspection.

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:09.380
Security measures include accurate inventory, controlled physical access,

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:13.835
protected cabinets and wiring, documented calibration, approved configuration tools,

00:01:13.835 --> 00:01:17.395
and monitoring of unexpected device or communication changes.

00:01:17.395 --> 00:01:21.230
Safety protections and fail-safe behavior should be engineered independently rather than

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.393
assumed to come from cybersecurity controls.

00:01:23.393 --> 00:01:26.395
Field devices remind us why ICS security is operational.

00:01:26.395 --> 00:01:30.730
A digital message can open a valve, start a motor, or change an electrical state.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:34.840
Defenders must understand the device function, expected operating range, failure mode,

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.920
and safe response before recommending actions.
